questions.worked_solution:
Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\ ⟨10,17,9⟩ & =3T(q)+⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\ 3T(q) & =⟨10,17,9⟩-⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\ 3T(q) & =⟨18,0,6⟩ \\ T(q) & =\frac{1}{3}⟨18,0,6⟩ \\ T(q) & =⟨6,0,2⟩.\end{aligned}
$$
